1
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:29,780
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:33,540
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:40,060
Target planet on maximum
telefinder range in 5, 4, 3,

4
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,797
2, 1.

5
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:42,800
Here it comes.

6
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:48,300
Hey guys, this could be it.

7
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,657
Sure looks promising this
time, don't you think?

8
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:52,657
I have a good feeling about this.

9
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:55,077
I think that planet is
going to be our new home.

10
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:57,557
According to our preliminary
observational data,

11
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:59,537
it seems to be reasonably similar to home.

12
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,897
Enough with the scientific crap already.

13
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:03,237
I say we take a chance.

14
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:04,497
Let's land this puppy.

15
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:06,097
We've done the cold sleep five times.

16
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:09,004
If we get frozen one more
time, we'll swivel up.

17
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:10,450
Knock it off.

18
00:02:10,533 --> 00:02:11,757
You're such a pig, Steve.

19
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:14,037
It's impossible to
settle here, and besides,

20
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:17,708
whether we land or not, that's
not a decision for us to make.

21
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:22,017
It definitely has a habitable environment,
but it has no existing oceans,

22
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:24,237
and its stratum consists mostly of quartz.

23
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,496
It's not worth waking up the old men.

24
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:32,597
Hey, Joey, just out of curiosity, what
kind of flowers are on that planet?

25
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,510
Huh?

26
00:02:33,593 --> 00:02:34,423
Uh, well...

27
00:02:34,506 --> 00:02:36,117
Weren't you listening to
what I said before, Rem?

28
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,157
That planet doesn't have...

29
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,070
Hold on.

30
00:02:38,153 --> 00:02:38,983
Why not?

31
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:40,873
We don't know that yet.

32
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:43,657
We'll decide once the results
of the minute analysis are in.

33
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:47,457
For all we know, it just might
have the flowers Rem thinks it has.

34
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:50,305
If it does, I sure hope
they'll be red flowers.

35
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:03,615
You're still in here?

36
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:04,962
Where's Knives?

37
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:10,160
I was wondering, why
don't they ever wake up?

38
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:12,757
This ship is too quiet.

39
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,780
It's just you and me and Knives.

40
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:18,746
And even with the rest of the
crew, there are only seven of us.

41
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,477
All right, Vash.

42
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:24,557
The day has finally come to tell you what
is written on the outside of this ship.

43
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,540
It says, Project Seeds.

44
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,100
Project Seeds? Yes.

45
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:32,897
These ships are like seeds that
are filled with our own genes.

46
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:34,509
Genes from the human race.

47
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:38,177
They are sent off to discover
and populate an unknown world.

48
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:42,378
I suppose you could say that we are
the caretakers of all those seeds.

49
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:45,637
If there's a god in deep space, he
must be laughing at us right now.

50
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:49,937
Our pitiful struggle for immortality must
look like an impossible quest to him.

51
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:52,617
Even though it may look shameful
to others, it represents.

52
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:57,220
For all of us, the desperate human will
to survive, to carry on our species.

53
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:01,499
When they arrive, a fight
on a new land awaits them.

54
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:05,137
This ship is their home,
and until it's time,

55
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:07,377
it's our job to let them sleep in peace.

56
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:10,107
Rem, is there anything
we can do to help you?

57
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:13,277
Oh, that's where you are.

58
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:17,184
So do you want to have lunch in
the usual place, in the rec room?

59
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,729
You really like that song.

60
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:29,437
It seems to pop into my
head whenever I'm happy.

61
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:30,637
Do you think it's strange?

62
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:31,597
No, not really.

63
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:32,557
It's a nice song.

64
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:33,470
That's sweet.

65
00:04:33,553 --> 00:04:34,383
Thanks, Knives.

66
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:38,200
It's weird.

67
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:40,057
Nothing's actually been moved around.

68
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:44,316
But every time we come here this
place seems different for some reason?

69
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,929
That's because it's alive!

70
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:47,957
Can't you feel it?

71
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,257
It has its own rhythm.

72
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:52,137
You can actually feel the
living part of the plan.

73
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:54,573
There she goes again thinking about home

74
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:59,077
So this looks like the world you
and the others keep talking about?

75
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:02,357
Well sort of but the scenery
at home was actually much more

76
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:05,734
expansive with a lot more
variety of plants and animals.

77
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,671
I'd like to see that Rem.

78
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:10,037
We're not just going to see
it We're going to create it.

79
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,591
We'll find a place to create our new home.

80
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,134
And when we get there?

81
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:19,040
There will be nothing but peaceful
days, with no war and no stealing.

82
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:24,149
An Eden where people can live
in freedom and harmony, right?

83
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:31,128
The state of our home, Earth, was so
desperate, we had no choice but to leave.

84
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:33,517
Mankind could no longer survive there.

85
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:35,894
The entire population was facing death,

86
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:39,497
so Project SEES was drafted as
a way to resolve this crisis.

87
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:42,404
Rem, that's our ship, the
one you told us about.

88
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,497
Judging from the computer data,

89
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:47,637
it looks to me like mankind is
responsible for damaging the planet.

90
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,602
Right, Captain?

91
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:50,337
I hate to say it, but it's true.

92
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:53,377
Our young race believed the land
and resources were unlimited,

93
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:54,977
which led to gradual destruction.

94
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:57,537
By the time they realized what
they had done, it was too late.

95
00:05:57,620 --> 00:05:59,277
The planet could no longer take the abuse.

96
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:03,517
If that's true, why did they come up with
the idea to set this project in motion?

97
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,820
The need to survive. Exactly.

98
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,397
The behavior of clinging to life till the

99
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:10,737
verge of death is
intrinsic to all organisms.

100
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:14,017
Survival instincts take over
dismissing shame in order to live.

101
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:17,453
But is it right to live if it
means such huge sacrifices?

102
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:21,357
We make the smallest sacrifice
we can think of at the time.

103
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:24,457
Unlike the other organisms on
the planet, we possess logic.

104
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:26,893
The knowledge to minimize the sacrifice.

105
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:30,417
Also, as human beings, we have
the ability to right our wrongs.

106
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:33,657
Hopefully, we'll learn from our
mistakes and start over in a new home.

107
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:34,570
As we journey,

108
00:06:34,653 --> 00:06:36,357
we need to take time to
search and think of ways to

109
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:39,734
make everyone happy without
endangering our environment.

110
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:42,940
This is no good.

111
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:45,057
What are you talking about?

112
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:47,057
I'm not cut out to be an educator.

113
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:48,611
What was I thinking, Rem?

114
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:51,397
I can only teach them
how to use the computer.

115
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,657
I've never been a father.

116
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:54,717
I don't know the first
thing about raising kids.

117
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:56,077
That goes double for me.

118
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:57,220
No, I'm serious.

119
00:06:57,540 --> 00:07:00,577
You're teaching them all sorts
of things, like emotions,

120
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:03,697
how to be kind to others,
and the value of the future.

121
00:07:03,780 --> 00:07:05,477
I'm not that great, Joey, really.

122
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:06,977
I just play with them, that's all.

123
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:08,060
It's no big deal.

124
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:13,465
Yeah, I guess we just have a
different way of looking at things.

125
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:18,297
You know, I was thinking, why do
you suppose they came here anyway?

126
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:20,320
Because they're angels. Angels?

127
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:23,077
Perhaps we should pay
more attention to them.

128
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:26,757
Bash and Knives could be angels God
sent to point us in the right direction.

129
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,252
They may even guide us through our dream.

130
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:37,840
Hey, Rem here?

131
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:40,453
No, she's with the kids in the rec room.

132
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,757
Like there isn't a care in the world.

133
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:46,177
Apparently she doesn't realize we
still have three plants left to adjust.

134
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:47,317
Oh yes, I meant to tell you.

135
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,897
The two little guys took care
of those while you were napping.

136
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:50,810
What?

137
00:07:50,893 --> 00:07:52,357
Tell me you're kidding, Rowan.

138
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:54,557
I'm fast, but that's still
a two-day job for me.

139
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:55,637
What's with them?

140
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,197
It's nothing to be surprised about.

141
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:58,797
Their IQ is way above ours.

142
00:07:58,880 --> 00:07:59,837
Don't take it so personally.

143
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,817
You should be glad
they're willing to help.

144
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:04,197
Maybe they're better suited
for brain work than you, Steve.

145
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,037
You need to lighten up
on those kids a little.

146
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:06,950
Cut the crap!

147
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:11,145
Do you really want the ship left
in the hands of those monsters?

148
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,837
Just look at how big
they grew in one year.

149
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:14,861
It isn't normal.

150
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:17,317
Those kids are monsters, I tell you.

151
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,230
Monsters!

152
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:25,490
Vash. Vash.

153
00:08:25,573 --> 00:08:27,320
Hey, you're crying again.

154
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,539
What's the matter?

155
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:31,290
It's Steve.

156
00:08:31,373 --> 00:08:32,617
He says that we're not human.

157
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:33,720
He hates me.

158
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:41,917
I know it's hard to understand, but to
these people, we're just uninvited guests.

159
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,757
We only need to be patient for a
little while until they accept us.

160
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,657
But Rem said that we could stay here.

161
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:49,277
Do you think she feels that way?

162
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:50,860
Remember what Joey said?

163
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:54,397
We have to make the smallest
sacrifice we can think of at the time.

164
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:57,245
If we can do that, we
can get through anything.

165
00:08:57,560 --> 00:09:00,207
Hey, Vash, do you know
why plants can't talk?

166
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:03,137
Rem said it's because
they're stronger than we are.

167
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:06,357
She said they're so strong, they
concentrate all their energy on living,

168
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:08,297
so they don't need to use words.

169
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:10,157
Yeah, they're strong,
but we eat their fruit.

170
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:12,299
We have to eat their fruit to live.

171
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:15,198
Do you think I'll be eating someday?

172
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:17,800
No, Knives, definitely not.

173
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:19,337
At least according to Rem.

174
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:20,297
Don't you remember?

175
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:22,917
She said they're making
a different kind of Eden.

176
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:23,830
Knives!

177
00:09:23,913 --> 00:09:25,738
What the hell are you doing in here?

178
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:30,017
This place is off limits to your kind.

179
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:31,394
You got that, monster?

180
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:36,460
So then why am I here?

181
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:46,170
Don't!

182
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,308
There's got to be a reason.

183
00:09:52,820 --> 00:09:54,840
Knives, it won't be much longer.

184
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:56,580
Take your time.

185
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:00,797
This is turning into quite a trim.

186
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:03,557
I never noticed before,
but you're really handsome.

187
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:04,470
Really?

188
00:10:04,553 --> 00:10:05,383
You think so, Rem?

189
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:07,170
Hey!

190
00:10:07,253 --> 00:10:08,520
I have an idea, handsome.

191
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:10,760
It's sticking up.

192
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:12,738
I think it's great.

193
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:14,369
It really suits you, Vash.

194
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:18,340
and it reminds me of him.

195
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:20,130
Who?

196
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:23,458
Someone I loved very much back home.

197
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:25,092
So where is he now, Rem?

198
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:28,040
He is in the land of angels, heaven.

199
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:30,540
He was my emotional support.

200
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:34,377
Thanks to him, I was able to face
my mistakes without judgment.

201
00:10:34,460 --> 00:10:36,177
I learned to make them right again.

202
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:39,277
Then I lost him and realized
that I would have to do it alone.

203
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:41,437
But I wasn't afraid to
make mistakes anymore.

204
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:45,991
I believed I could point myself in the
right direction without looking back.

205
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:52,240
That is exactly why I got on this ship,
so I could enter the future as I am.

206
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:55,380
Rem, are you sad?

207
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:57,580
Well, just a little.

208
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,280
You know, you have me.

209
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:02,132
I won't leave you alone.

210
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:06,680
I promise I won't, because
I really love you, Rem.

211
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:10,380
You're such a baby.

212
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:13,180
But thank you, Vash.

213
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,118
Anyway, we're done.

214
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,456
Shall we switch now?

215
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:18,170
Knives!

216
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:28,160
It's all wrong!

217
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,976
Hey, somehow I knew you'd be in here.

218
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:38,000
What happened?

219
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,652
Just a small change of heart, that's all.

220
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:45,035
Besides, if we stay the same,
there's no individuality.

221
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:02,820
That's a wonderful
haircut, Knives! Thank you.

222
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:06,400
As strange as it may sound,
I actually feel refreshed.

223
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:09,737
You know, you look very intellectual.

224
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:12,137
Why, you look like a
regular little philosopher.

225
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:13,396
What do I look like?

226
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:15,720
A mama's boy. That's me.

227
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:18,710
Huh?

228
00:12:18,793 --> 00:12:23,540
I'm amazed you can stomach eating at the
same table with those little monsters.

229
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:27,537
Steve, I think you've had one too many.

230
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:29,080
No, I haven't, baby.

231
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:30,897
Hey, Steve, come on.

232
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:33,277
Don't you have some work you
still have to do someplace else?

233
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:35,237
Oh, shut up, Poindexter.

234
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:36,908
I can always do that later.

235
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,197
You're a disgrace.

236
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:39,110
Huh?

237
00:12:39,193 --> 00:12:40,023
Now,

238
00:12:40,106 --> 00:12:41,257
is that any way for a
grown man like you to

239
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:43,928
behave in the presence
of innocent children?

240
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:52,856
He sure has been acting crazy lately.

241
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:55,171
It's because he's afraid.

242
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:03,865
Who does he think he is draping
himself all over Mary like that?

243
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:08,200
Those two are such a pain.

244
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:12,112
But then again, I suppose just
one would be rather boring.

245
00:13:33,900 --> 00:13:34,730
Oh

246
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:38,096
That was the easiest way to stop him.

247
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:39,997
You wanted to save the butterfly, right?

248
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,997
I Didn't want to kill the spider.

249
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,609
I wanted to save them both

250
00:13:43,940 --> 00:13:46,157
What are you talking about
unless the spider caught

251
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:48,537
the butterfly it would
die of starvation anyway?

252
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:49,900
You can't save both.

253
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:51,217
Don't you know that?

254
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:53,947
It's not right to make
that choice so easily.

255
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:56,377
Both of them are living creatures knives,

256
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:58,897
so you should but I'm not
wrong about this realm!

257
00:13:58,980 --> 00:14:02,117
If you just keep saving the
butterflies the spiders will die?

258
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,030
Yes, but...

259
00:14:03,113 --> 00:14:05,617
Wanting to save both is
just a naive contradiction.

260
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:07,657
And what would you have rather had us do?

261
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:09,017
Just stand and think about it?

262
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:12,924
In the meantime, while we do that,
the spider eats the butterfly.

263
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,308
What's wrong with you, Nye?

264
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:17,420
Don't you understand?

265
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:20,392
I wanted to save both of them, you idiot!

266
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:34,280
You don't make any sense, Bash.

267
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:37,020
I don't think so, Knives!

268
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:39,631
You're the one who doesn't make any sense!

269
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:46,220
According to interplanetary
law, Steve is relieved of duty.

270
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:48,519
He will be detained in the freezer.

271
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:51,477
Furthermore, upon the
completion of our mission,

272
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:54,197
he will be released from
detention to stand trial.

273
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:55,110
That is all.

274
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,177
All I did was get a little drunk!

275
00:14:57,260 --> 00:14:58,777
Why can't you believe what I'm saying?

276
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:00,237
We haven't heard his side yet.

277
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:01,477
You're not being fair to him.

278
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:05,089
I saw him go into Mary's room,
and I find that unacceptable.

279
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:06,330
Hey, wait!

280
00:15:06,413 --> 00:15:07,435
I didn't do anything!

281
00:15:07,700 --> 00:15:09,960
We still have time to discuss this.

282
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:13,277
In order for us to function
as a group, we need law.

283
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,242
It protects all of us from harm.

284
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:17,357
The entire team must understand this.

285
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:21,857
But maybe it wouldn't hurt to hear his
side of the story before we freeze him!

286
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:23,780
Rem, he raped me.

287
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:25,490
No!

288
00:15:25,573 --> 00:15:26,640
I didn't do it!

289
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:33,497
Rem, why can't everyone just
get along with each other?

290
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:37,521
I suppose it's because people have
many different ways of thinking.

291
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:39,357
But even if we do make mistakes,

292
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:43,177
we have the ability to do something about
it and make better choices the next time.

293
00:15:43,260 --> 00:15:46,677
And if you keep your vision
clear, you will see the future.

294
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:49,880
What happens in our future
is our own responsibility.

295
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,030
Marry you?

296
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:54,870
You.

297
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,557
Come on, you must be teasing.

298
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:59,577
As soon as we're finished here,
I'd like you to come to the bridge.

299
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:02,317
The analysis should be in
in just a little while.

300
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:05,224
I made sure that Steve
will never wake up again.

301
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:07,111
I readjusted the freezer.

302
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:09,580
I didn't mean for us to kill him!

303
00:16:10,660 --> 00:16:12,895
I guess now that means we're partners.

304
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:18,870
Joey!

305
00:16:18,953 --> 00:16:19,959
What's wrong, Rem?

306
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:23,020
The A-12 monitors.

307
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:24,868
Somebody disconnected them.

308
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:36,760
It's her own fault. I had no choice.

309
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:38,937
I helped her and then she betrayed me.

310
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:41,608
I was only trying to
protect her from Steve.

311
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:44,020
Rowan, please don't.

312
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:47,105
She even told me she loved me.

313
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,617
There's simply no excuse.

314
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:50,340
Rem, you do understand me.

315
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:55,180
Oh, I see now.

316
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,220
It had to be him.

317
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:59,157
Because of him, Mary had to die.

318
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:00,240
It was his fault.

319
00:17:00,660 --> 00:17:02,317
What are you talking about, Rowan?

320
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:03,812
Please put the gun down!

321
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:06,600
Rem, what's happening? Rem! Rem!

322
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:09,397
He can't get away with it, that monster.

323
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:10,656
I have to shoot him.

324
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:13,907
Now get out of the way, Rem!

325
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:19,817
No one has the right to
take the life of another.

326
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:21,488
You don't want to kill him.

327
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:22,640
Now put it down.

328
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:23,899
It's not too late.

329
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:26,180
Stay! Stay! Stay!

330
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:30,340
Rowan, what are you doing?

331
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,237
Something's broken inside me.

332
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,150
I'm done.

333
00:17:33,233 --> 00:17:34,820
I can't seem to stop.

334
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,500
It's all right, Rowan.

335
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:38,414
Rem, get out of there!

336
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:39,990
Rem!

337
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:43,180
It's not too late to start over.

338
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:44,710
Here.

339
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:49,100
Please stay back, Rem.

340
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:52,100
Don't make me shoot you!

341
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,780
No, Rowan, nooo!

342
00:18:09,780 --> 00:18:11,309
Why did you do that, Joey?

343
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,318
If I hadn't, he would have shot you.

344
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,657
I'm sorry, there was no other way.

345
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:18,799
I knew Rowan, he wouldn't shoot me.

346
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:22,953
Please understand, I couldn't
see that from the monitors.

347
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:25,500
I had to decide quickly. If I hadn't...

348
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:29,610
Rowan...

349
00:18:29,693 --> 00:18:30,523
Mary...

350
00:18:30,606 --> 00:18:31,436
Joey, I agree with you.

351
00:18:31,519 --> 00:18:33,693
I think you did exactly the right thing.

352
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:34,837
Rowan went crazy.

353
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,332
That's all you could do.

354
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:37,877
That's what I thought.

355
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,489
But what if Rem was right?

356
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:41,197
Perhaps he wasn't going to shoot her.

357
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:43,817
If that's true, what I did
was a horrible mistake.

358
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:46,429
You're just a human,
like the rest of them.

359
00:18:48,220 --> 00:18:50,220
I know my choice is the right one.

360
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:55,364
Altering ship's course program.

361
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,080
What is it?

362
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:00,497
We're changing direction.

363
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:01,897
Our course has been re-entered.

364
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:02,810
What?

365
00:19:02,893 --> 00:19:04,957
Someone is sending orders
to all of the ships.

366
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:08,640
All systems are now operating
on auto-lock mode. Oh, my God.

367
00:19:08,840 --> 00:19:11,597
At this rate, the ships are
going to crash on that planet.

368
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:14,177
Apparently, Rowan had started
up the orbital program.

369
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:15,480
We have to evacuate.

370
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:16,830
Where's Joey?

371
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:19,417
He told me to get us to the escape pods.

372
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:20,817
He said he'd try to save the ships.

373
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:23,800
But what about all the
sleeping people on board?

374
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:25,117
We can't worry about that.

375
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:26,906
We've got to get out of here.

376
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:28,100
Rem, come on.

377
00:19:28,620 --> 00:19:30,320
We have to go to the pods.

378
00:19:31,260 --> 00:19:32,660
Warning. Warning.

379
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:35,517
This ship is about to
enter the atmosphere.

380
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:37,600
Please proceed to the escape pods.

381
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:40,300
Please proceed to the escape pods.

382
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:45,380
Come on.

383
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:47,091
You've got to hurry, Rem.

384
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:49,760
A fight on a new land awaits them.

385
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:52,337
We're not going to see it,
we're going to create it.

386
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:55,737
And if you keep your vision
clear, you will see the future.

387
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:58,938
What happens in our future
is our own responsibility.

388
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:00,993
Ram, what's the matter?

389
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:04,440
Alex, help me. Give me strength.

390
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,056
You two go on ahead.

391
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:09,317
I don't understand what you mean.

392
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:10,230
Why?

393
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:12,597
I can't leave Joey here by himself.

394
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:15,317
And I have to try to find
a way to save the others.

395
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:17,217
But the program is already running.

396
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:18,537
You've got to come with us, Ram.

397
00:20:18,620 --> 00:20:20,040
Please don't leave us!

398
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,360
I'm sorry, Vash.

399
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:25,757
If Alex were still alive, I believe in
my heart that he would do the same thing.

400
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:27,369
Vash, take care of knives!

401
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:31,260
Don't worry, Vash.

402
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:52,720
No, Rem!

403
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,480
No, you can't leave!

404
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,440
Please come back, Rem!

405
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:01,580
I'll never understand humans.

406
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:03,077
They're a total waste of life.

407
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:06,677
To think they'd actually sacrifice themselves
out of foolish sentiment for others.

408
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:08,054
It's incomprehensible.

409
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:12,017
I thought I'd let her live only
because you were so attached to her.

410
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:14,982
But now I see how truly
imperfect she really was.

411
00:21:15,220 --> 00:21:16,808
It's a good thing she died.

412
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:18,300
Don't say that!

413
00:21:19,060 --> 00:21:21,037
Their immigration is out of the question.

414
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:24,577
That'd be like spreading pathogenic
organisms across our healthy universe.

415
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:27,420
You're saying you planned
this? That's right.

416
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:30,333
But don't worry, you and I will be fine.

417
00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:32,517
I made sure the planned ship will survive.

418
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,577
After all, we need that
to create our new home.

419
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:36,497
Now, won't we, my dearest brother?

420
00:21:36,580 --> 00:21:39,540
Only ships carrying the humans will crash.

421
00:21:40,160 --> 00:21:40,990
Ah!

422
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:42,500
Bring them back!

423
00:21:42,700 --> 00:21:44,406
Bring them back, you bastard!

424
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:49,800
All ships now commencing
orbital correction.

425
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:53,900
Reverse thrusters.

426
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:56,840
That bitch actually did it.

427
00:21:58,020 --> 00:21:59,540
I'm sorry, Rem.

428
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:21,040
Vash, take care of knives.

429
00:22:28,460 --> 00:22:29,657
Trust me, Rem.

430
00:22:29,740 --> 00:22:32,077
I will...

431
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:33,900
take care of him.

432
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,317
Thank

433
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:05,717
you

434
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:12,417
so

435
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:15,960
much for watching.

436
00:23:42,380 --> 00:23:47,920
Aishita o mitsumete Mary

437
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:13,280
shining down upon us from the
skies, stained red with blood.

438
00:24:14,500 --> 00:24:16,912
And let us remember his name, his legend.

439
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:19,219
To do so, you only need to look up.

440
00:24:19,620 --> 00:24:22,857
Like it or not, his legend is
chiseled into the fifth moon,

441
00:24:22,940 --> 00:24:25,380
a permanent etching from a terrible past.

442
00:24:26,460 --> 00:24:29,980
The legend of Vash the
Stampede, chiseled forever.

443
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:34,157
And then the time comes, you
only need to tell of the tracks,

444
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:35,760
which lead to the future.
